  {
    "episode_id": 48662,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48662.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, a lot of the things he talked about in his America First Agenda are things that we're trying to put in the budget reconciliation bill. There are a lot of limitations on budget reconciliation. One thing that is if there is anything easy to do in budget reconciliation, it's tax policy because it definitely has a budget nexus. But outside of budget reconciliation, President Trump talked about Several issues that I think hit home in Arkansas. He talked about more domestic steel production and Arkansas is now, I believe, leading the country in steel production. That's not in my district, but it's in Arkansas and that makes us all proud. He talked about more domestic lumber production. That's definitely in my district. There's opportunity for us to do a lot more of that. I guess you saw her warehouser has announced a $500 million new plant down in Drew County. That's very encouraging. And then he also talked about the Golden Dome, which a lot of those components in the high altitude missile defense system will be made down in Camden, also in the Fourth District at the Highland Industrial Park. So all of those things along with the energy, I think Arkansas has got tremendous energy potential, the lithium deposits and the role that that plays in the energy sector. I really see a bright future for Arkansas with the things that President Trump talked about in his State of the Union address.",
